WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.770
I won't lose either!

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:03.980
Matatagi?

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.530
Parkour Attack!

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.460
I am not... scared of failing!

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:30.240
I did it!

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.880
Good job, Sakura!

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.950
Inazuma Japan rides on their momentum!

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.590
Will they be able to keep this up to the end?!

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:46.590
Are you telling me that this team is actually incredibly powerful?

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.910
The quarterfinals are next.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:57.410
Three more matches to win the Asia district prelims.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.910
We'll definitely make it to the world's field!

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.050
Let's practice hard for today!

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:43.660
Okay!

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:47.560
I think you've all grown really accustomed to soccer after our two matches.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.150
So today's practice is going to be more practical.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:52.810
Practical?

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:57.310
We'll divide into offense and defense and imagine ourselves in a real match.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.750
You won't just be kicking the ball.

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:03.950
You'll also be thinking of things such as where you should move next as you play.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.220
Shindou-san, please join the defense.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.180
Okay.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.670
Sakura, Kusaka, and I will be joining Matatagi and the other forwards in offense.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:13.920
Leave it to me!

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:16.380
All right then, let's start!

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.260
I'll block all the shots!

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.570
Here I go!

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:29.180
Matatagi!

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.270
I'll stop you!

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.160
Nozaki-san!

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:40.780
It's mine!

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.640
Good job, Sakura!

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.160
Nice pass, Matatagi!

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.580
I'll get even better at this!

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:50.660
Captain!

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.480
Sakura-san sure has changed.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.100
She was always a cheerful person, but now she looks so much more alive.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:03:59.800
Indeed.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.330
Over here, here!

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.930
I don't know where "here" is!

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.260
Give me more precise directions!

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:20.820
More precise...?

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.720
You're so slow!

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.370
It's not my fault...

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.030
Minaho! Manabe!

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:30.910
Don't worry about it! We'll rebound!

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.820
R-Right!

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:33.410
Yeah!

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:38.280
It's progressing little by little, but everyone is coming together.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:40.880
This team can do it!

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:42.630
Kusaka!

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:47.440
Close one!

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:48.470
You had a good flow going there!

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:56.730
Tsurugi!

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:00.150
Bring it!

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.440
I'll stop it this time!

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:09.530
Are you okay?

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.310
Yeah...

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:22.210
Okay, let's end here for today's practice!

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.550
Everyone, rest up for tomorrow!

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:26.720
Okay!

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.200
Good work today.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:30.930
Thanks.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.460
They're improving, don't you think?

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:35.220
Yeah.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:36.890
They're all enjoying soccer.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:41.750
I think with these members, we'll be able to put up a fight against the world!

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.150
I wouldn't say that.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:49.160
They may have gotten more or less better, but they're still beginners.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:51.120
Shindou-san...

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:59.870
But it was Matatagi's speed and Sakura's pass that helped us score the tying shoot with Korea and the winning goal against Australia, isn't it?

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:05.150
Also, Ibuki blocked a shoot in the Australia match.

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:09.110
Regardless.

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:11.140
Ibuki still has much to improve on as goalkeeper,

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:15.960
and Minaho, Manabe, and Morimura's abilities are still unknown.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:20.240
Kusaka can't even receive a pass properly yet.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:21.360
Maybe, but...!

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.090
Tenma.

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:24.730
The world isn't that easy.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:37.820
<i>Tenma.</i>

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:39.620
<i>The world isn't that easy.</i>

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.550
Nanase... Gotanda... Ropponmatsu...

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:58.850
I swear, I'll protect you guys!

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:09.780
Our opponent for the quarterfinals has been determined.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:13.270
It's Saudi Arabia's team, Shamshir.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:23.060
Their speed and destructive power, not only individually but also as a unified team, is near number one champion in offense.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:26.660
Their play style involves persistently attacking their opponent's weakpoints until they're brought down.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:30.230
Thus, they are feared as Arabia's lions.

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:34.470
Arabia's lions, huh?

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.330
Starting tomorrow, we will make last adjustments for our Saudi match.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:43.480
For now, you are dismissed. Spend the rest of your day freely.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:49.940
Use this opportunity to absorb yourselves in things other than soccer.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.930
A break, huh...

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:00.430
It feels like we haven't had one of those in a while.

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:01.750
What are you all going to do?

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.400
I'm staying in bed.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:12.200
With practice tomorrow starting at 8A.M.,  I'll have 22 hours and 37 minutes of sleep.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:16.680
That ought to restore me from 97% of the stress that I have collected.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:20.220
I'm going for a run around the place.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:23.650
I feel sluggish if I don't keep my body moving.

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:28.190
I'm going back home for a bit to check on my brothers.

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:30.400
What about you, Konoha?

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:35.660
If you don't have plans, then want to go to the Soccer Garden's shopping mall with me?

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:40.910
Okay...

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:42.250
Tsurugi!

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:45.460
Help me out with practice.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:47.960
All right. {いいとも！}

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.210
Kusaka!

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.470
Want to practice together?

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:56.620
That's okay.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:09:00.060
You don't have to spend your time on someone like me.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.220
Bye.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:10.900
Shun!

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:12.860
Oh, Nii-chan!

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:16.200
What happened to your face?

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.330
Kenta did it.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:22.640
When I hid his monster toy, he got mad and hit me.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:23.910
Come on, Shun.

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:26.800
Aren't I always telling you?

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:29.640
Whatever it is you do, don't get caught doing it.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.650
If you get found out, you lose.

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:35.040
If you don't get caught doing something, you win.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:35.670
Got that?

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:38.180
Yeah!

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:42.680
I'm not done yet!

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.680
Don't hold back!

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:45.140
Bring it!

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:50.980
One more time!

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:20.010
This mall is flourishing better than I expected.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:23.970
By the way, Konoha, under what terms were you hired for?

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:30.900
I joined so I could study abroad in the world's best rhythmic gymnastics team.

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:36.000
The school I'm from was too low-level for me.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:36.860
That's why...

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.240
That's why, I have to be at the top no matter what.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:50.810
Is there anything fun we can do?

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:54.080
Yo, Kusaka.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:57.050
I hear you're kicking balls around lately?

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:05.400
Arabia's lions, huh...

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:08.040
Their power certainly is destructive.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.940
Bad news, Tenma!

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:11.550
Kusaka-kun...

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:12.980
Kusaka-kun got arrested by the police!

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:15.940
Arrested?

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:20.540
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:26.370
Tsurugi, a new pack came out! When should we play?

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:28.580
Now!

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:35.040
There are so many cards I've never seen before!

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:37.240
There's 100 types in total!

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:38.550
Wow!

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:41.630
From here on, all you need are cards to battle!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.550
All right then! Let's fight!

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:47.930
Fly to the world! New Inazuma Japan!

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:50.930
Check out the Kickoff Starter Deck, too!

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:55.580
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:58.610
Arrested?

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:00.150
What happened?

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.330
He got into a fight with some punks in town.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.530
Fight? Why?

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.420
Now that I think about it...

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:09.500
Even in our exhibition match with Teikoku...

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.250
<i>Did you just call me weak?!</i>

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:14.880
<i>Did you?!</i>

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:22.480
I don't believe this!

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:25.280
Off-field violence at such an important time for us!

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:28.680
Well, I always had a feeling he would pull something like this.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:33.900
That's why I was against adding that delinquent to the team!

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:38.300
Coach, I'm not finished talking to-

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:43.950
Coach!

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:48.060
You're going to the police station, right?

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:49.490
Please take me with you.

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:52.450
Have it your way.

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:03.920
Kusaka-san, how long are we going to keep this up?

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:06.430
What do you mean?

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:10.770
Well, I was wondering what we're doing all this for.

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:14.640
We have to protect our team.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.730
Protect our team's what?

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.750
Our turf? Our pride?

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:24.240
Instead of protecting, doesn't it seem more like you're just ruining everyone's life?

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.720
This way.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:30.580
Kusaka...

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:38.080
Um...

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:42.550
Aren't you going to reprimand me or something?

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:45.510
Do you want me to?

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:49.270
No... not exactly...

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:00.620
We heard the news, Captain.

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:03.740
Kusaka got arrested?

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:05.910
Y-Yeah...

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:07.070
So, how did it go?

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:11.530
For the time being, Coach identified himself as his guardian and brought him back.

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:13.170
I see...

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:15.040
Thank goodness it didn't turn into anything big.

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:18.000
What are you all doing here anyway?

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:21.880
The truth is, we got to wondering and checked up on several things.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:25.110
Kusaka-kun is actually quite a dangerous person.

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:30.510
He caused a problem at his school, so he and his friends are expelled from school right now.

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:34.520
At that school, he was a delinquent who controlled the baddest of the bad kids.

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:41.640
Normally he has the kind face of Buddha, but once he loses his temper he changes into a demon.

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:48.450
The dragon "ryuu" character that's in his name earned him the nickname "The Dragon With Two Faces" in that school. {鬼仏のリュウ}

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:55.730
His terms for being hired by Coach Kuroiwa is that both he and his friends be reinstated back into their school.

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:58.040
But it's strange.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.210
I went back even further in my investigations about him,

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:07.550
and apparently years ago, he was a very kind person who was more of a scaredy cat than someone who got angry easily.

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:12.510
But after a certain incident, he suddenly changed into a whole different person.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:14.840
Incident?

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:16.060
What happened?

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.240
I don't know that much...

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:22.830
Either way, Kusaka is going to be dropped from Inazuma Japan.

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:26.480
Trainer Funagi came in earlier to tell us that.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:29.220
That's inevitable.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:34.360
It didn't develop into anything serious this time, but what about the next time?

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:40.220
It would be horrible if he causes another problem for us and ends up withdrawing from the team anyway.

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:41.580
He can't do that!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.660
I'm going to have a talk with Trainer Funagi.

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:45.790
Tenma.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.550
Why are you defending Kusaka that much?

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:51.900
Why...?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:02.060
Anyway, I'm going to Trainer Funagi!

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:04.250
Tenma!

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:11.730
I won't let them make Kusaka quit!

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:14.990
Coach...

00:16:16.220 --> 00:16:19.740
Kusaka will be remaining on this team.

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:24.320
Coach...

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:35.040
<i>Protect the team's what?</i>

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:39.680
<i>Instead of protecting, doesn't it seem more like you're just ruining everyone's life?</i>

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:51.660
The quarterfinals for FFI's Vision 2 Asia district preliminaries is here at last!

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:57.260
Today I bring to you the match between Japan's Inazuma Japan and Saudi Arabia's Shamshir!

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:01.910
Just look at that audience.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:05.310
Large crowds. Loud cheers.

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:06.880
This is gonna be fun.

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:14.800
Everyone, let's go!

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:16.130
Okay!

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:21.020
Inazuma Japan and Shamshir are both in position!

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:23.140
The match will begin momentarily!

00:17:23.530 --> 00:17:25.200
Nii-chan, you can do it!

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:26.520
You can do it!

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:33.490
Kusaka!

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:35.200
Let's give it all we've got.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.440
T-That's...

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:43.700
Sato-chan!

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:48.710
What is Sato-chan doing here...?

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.550
The match opens with Inazuma Japan's kickoff!

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.800
Shindou, not this again!

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:02.150
It's mine!

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:05.600
The ball is stolen from Matatagi right away!

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:07.730
I'll stop you!

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:10.310
They're fast!

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:12.690
Tamil!

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:14.190
Nazim!

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:17.570
Shamshir moves up in their attack!

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:21.150
Precise passes and above-average speed.

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:23.080
They're just as the rumors about them specified.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.080
But I won't let them take another step forward.

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:29.870
Einsatz!

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:33.750
Yes!

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:35.090
Nice one, Shindou-senpai!

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:36.620
What?!

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:39.260
Shamshir takes back the ball without a moment's delay!

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:43.600
They took the ball from Shindou-san so easily...

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:46.060
Sa'id!

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:52.150
Oil Rush!

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:58.640
It's in!

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:00.530
Shamshir makes the first goal!

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:04.030
What's up with that shoot...

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:10.060
The match between Inazuma Japan and Shamshir opens with Shamshir's fierce shoot!

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:13.040
I sure hope Inazuma Japan manages to catch up quickly!

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:17.570
Their power really is destructive, and their offense has no openings.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:21.110
But we have to win!

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:22.550
We have to combine everyone's strengths together!

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:28.350
The match resumes with Inazuma Japan's kickoff!

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.020
This is in the bag!

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:32.560
Pass to Kusaka!

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:38.780
Kusaka!

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:41.530
The ball is stolen from Inazuma Japan!

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:44.150
You call yourself a representative of Japan?

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:45.440
Don't make me laugh.

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:47.740
A weak guy like you?

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:50.040
Weak?

00:19:50.510 --> 00:19:53.130
Are you hard of hearing too, blockhead?

00:19:57.080 --> 00:19:58.840
Don't you underestimate me!

00:20:04.620 --> 00:20:06.310
F-Foul!

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:09.550
Kusaka makes a dangerous tackle on the opponent team!

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:11.430
W-What's this guy's problem?

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:20.740
Why...

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:23.510
Why are you doing this, Kusaka?

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:26.310
You practiced so hard!

00:20:26.310 --> 00:20:28.680
Don't you care if you can't get to play soccer anymore?!

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:31.250
Kusaka!

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:35.550
Kusaka-kun... you're scared, aren't you?

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:39.240
I can tell...

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:41.550
Because... I feel the same way...

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.560
Scared?

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:46.520
What would I be scared of?

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:55.060
I tried to protect Sato-chan back then...

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:56.690
But even though I tried...

00:20:57.170 --> 00:20:59.520
L-Let Sato-chan go!

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:02.490
Don't act tough when you're really weak.

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:05.840
I-I'm not weak...

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:07.550
I'm not weak!

00:21:08.460 --> 00:21:09.510
Dummy!

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:11.160
Let's get out of here.

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:24.330
You guys...

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:26.130
Wait right there!

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:34.480
Kusaka-kun is scared...

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:39.620
He's scared that if he isn't strong, everyone will leave him...

00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:42.030
I can tell...

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:45.530
Kusaka...

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:52.350
Now there's an interesting guy...

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:53.410
Yeah.

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:37.850
Next Episode

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:25.960
What does it mean to be strong?

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:27.420
What does it mean to be weak?

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:30.680
Kusaka! What sort of strength is it you're looking for?

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:33.050
Next, The Emperor's Tears!

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:35.350
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:45.080 --> 00:23:49.370
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:53.330 --> 00:23:55.940
The world isn't that easy!

00:23:56.170 --> 00:23:57.450
That's all!
